{"schema_version":3,"seq":43,"ts":"2026-11-08T20:37:09Z","type":"finding_annotated","finding":"F14","writers":["src/gateway.js:21"],"removers":["src/gateway.js:32"],"note":"Gateway.sessions (Map) entry is removed only in Gateway.release, which runs only on the socket 'close' event (gateway.js:25). Sessions closed server-side (bye, idle timeout, protocol error) go through Session.close, which clears the heartbeat timer and unsubscribes topics but never removes the session from Gateway.sessions; LoopbackSocket.destroy() does not emit 'close', so release never runs. Each retained entry keeps the Session, its socket, decoder, 64 recent messages and the data/close listeners. Hang-up-only workload (load.js) plateaus; bye workload grows (heap_used growth-continues after gc). Missing pairing: Session.close should deregister from the gateway (e.g. an onClose callback calling sessions.delete). Heartbeat timer is correctly cleared."}
